# Copy this file to .env and fill in your keys:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The bot loads .env automatically at startup (via python-dotenv).
# Exporting these variables in your shell still works exactly as before --
# shell environment variables take precedence over values in .env.
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit real keys.

# --- LLM API keys (set the ones for the LLMs you use) ---
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-gemini-key-here
CLAUDE_API_KEY=your-anthropic-key-here
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is also accepted as an alias for CLAUDE_API_KEY.
OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-key-here
XAI_API_KEY=your-grok-key-here
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=your-perplexity-key-here

# --- LLM model overrides (optional -- see modelregistry.py / MODELS.md) ---
# Model IDs are hardcoded nowhere else in the codebase; every call site
# reads them through modelregistry.get_model(), which checks these env
# vars first and falls back to the DEFAULT_MODELS registry. Set one of
# these to pin a specific model, or to work around a provider retiring
# the current default without waiting for a code change.
#GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-pro-preview
#CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
#OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.5
#GROK_MODEL=grok-4.5
#PERPLEXITY_MODEL=sonar-pro

# --- Trading (required even for what-if runs) ---
# The bot constructs the Coinbase client unconditionally on startup,
# regardless of trading mode, so this file is required for every run.
# Coinbase credentials JSON file (default: cdp_api_key.json, gitignored).
# Download this from the Coinbase Developer Platform and place it at the
# repo root; there is no env var for the key contents themselves, only for
# the path to the file.
#COINBASE_CREDENTIALS_FILE=cdp_api_key.json

# --- Optional data providers ---
#LUNARCRUSH_API_KEY=
#COINMARKETCAP_API_KEY=
# CMC_API_KEY is also accepted as an alias for COINMARKETCAP_API_KEY.

# --- Optional: additional data/DEX providers (all optional) ---
#COINGECKO_API_KEY=
#JUPITER_API_KEY=
#SOLANA_RPC_URL=

# !!! NEVER COMMIT WALLET SECRETS !!!
# SOLANA_PRIVATE_KEY and WALLET_MNEMONIC are directly spendable -- anyone
# who obtains them can drain the wallet. Keep them out of source control,
# logs, and any shared file. Treat them with the same care as a bank
# password, not like an ordinary API key.
#SOLANA_PRIVATE_KEY=
#WALLET_MNEMONIC=

# --- Optional run configuration (can also be passed as CLI flags) ---
# See OPERATIONS_MANUAL.md for the full list.
#TRADING_MODE=whatif
#LLM_MODE=compare
#PRIMARY_LLM=gemini
# Panel choice (COMPARE_LLMS) is a trade-frequency knob: consensus requires
# unanimity, so every added panelist makes BUY strictly rarer. The structured
# trio below is the recommended live-cadence default (fast, cheap, no
# fallback parsing). Add grok+perplexity (live web search, slower, pricier,
# ~unanimity-proof in quiet markets) for occasional deep what-if scans.
#COMPARE_LLMS=gemini,claude,openai
# ANALYZE_COINS: explicit coins to analyze (max 5); empty = discovery mode.
# TRAP: setting this counts as "explicit coins", which runs COIN CHOICE MODE and
# makes the filter/discovery flags (--chains/--categories/--polymarket-filter/
# --discovery) inert -- they only apply in discovery mode. The bot no longer
# ignores this silently: with ANALYZE_COINS set here, passing a filter/discovery
# flag on the CLI prints "[CONFIG] ... ignoring ANALYZE_COINS env" and runs the
# filter/discovery pass (CLI wins). Passing BOTH --coins= and a filter flag on
# the CLI is a hard [CONFIG ERROR]. To run filtered/discovery while this is set,
# just add the filter flags on the CLI, or leave ANALYZE_COINS empty.
#ANALYZE_COINS=

# !!! Do NOT put LIVE_TRADING_CONFIRMED=1 in this file. It is the env half
# of the live-trading double lock and must be typed in the shell per
# invocation (or via a deliberate shell alias) -- the bot strips and loudly
# ignores a .env-supplied value, so it will NOT arm live trading from here.
# Convenient live invocation: add to ~/.zshrc:
#   alias tradbot-live='LIVE_TRADING_CONFIRMED=1 ./venv/bin/python crypto_trading_bot.py --live --trading-mode=live'

# --- Spend caps (live trading; CLI flags override) ---
# TRADE_NOTIONAL_USD: USD per buy (default 5.00, hard ceiling 100.00).
# RUN_SPEND_CAP_USD: max cumulative intended spend per run (default 10.00).
# DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD: max cumulative LIVE spend per UTC day, summed from the
#   execution ledger across runs (default 15.00). What-if runs don't count.
# The startup banner and run summary show each cap and how much of today's
# daily cap is spent.
#
# The code defaults ($5/$10/$15) are acceptance-test scale: they validate the
# money path but at ~1.2%/side fees they can't produce meaningful P&L. A
# measured trading scale (matching the original bot's $25 orders): notional
# sets dollar stakes (fees are %-based, so it doesn't change the win
# threshold), the run cap sets fills-per-run, and the daily cap should be
# sized to how many open positions you can unwind BY HAND per day -- there is
# no automated sell path.
#TRADE_NOTIONAL_USD=25.00
#RUN_SPEND_CAP_USD=50.00
#DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD=100.00
